Sorry, but there have been rebuses on every day of the week. Very rare on Friday or Saturday, but they've been there. Thursday's the most common, and Wednesday and Sunday are the next two in line, then Tuesday and Monday. 

A lot of us like the added challenge of figuring out what's going on in a puzzle, and like having an unexpected issue to contend with. We don't think they're "unfair" at all, and this one was fairly obvious. I was happy to see an easy rebus today, and am looking forward to whatever's going to happen in the Thursday puzzle.

